# Captured live on 2026-10-12 from GNU inetutils telnet 2.8 (Arch Linux),
# TERM=xterm, in a 80x24 pseudo-terminal, against a loopback listener that sent
# kOS's connect sequence (WILL ECHO, DONT ECHO, WILL SGA, DO NAWS, DO TERMTYPE)
# and kOS's character-mode negotiation replies.
# Each read: line is one recv() from the client socket, in hex.
# Keys typed: 'print 1+1.', Enter, e-acute, Up arrow, Backspace (DEL), Ctrl-C;
# then the window grew to 100x30; then Ctrl-] quit closed the connection.
# Note: Enter arrives as CR NUL (RFC 854), the terminal type in upper case.
read: ff fd 01 ff fd 03 ff fb 1f ff fa 1f 00 50 00 18 ff f0 ff fb 18
read: ff fa 18 00 58 54 45 52 4d ff f0
# typing
read: 70 72 69 6e 74 20 31 2b 31 2e
read: 0d 00
read: c3 a9
read: 1b 5b 41
read: 7f
read: 03
# resize 30x100
read: ff fa 1f 00 64 00 1e ff f0
# close
eof
